  "notes": "USAGE:\nCan be used as a noun ({疎外|そがい}) or as a suru-verb ({疎外|そがい}する, to alienate/exclude). The passive form {疎外|そがい}される (to be alienated) is very common.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {疎外|そがい}{感|かん} (sense of alienation)\n- {社会的|しゃかいてき}{疎外|そがい} (social alienation)\n- {疎外|そがい}される (to be alienated, excluded)\n- {仲間|なかま}から{疎外|そがい}される (to be excluded from the group)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {孤立|こりつ}: isolation (being alone, may be voluntary)\n- {排除|はいじょ}: exclusion, removal (more active, deliberate act of removing)\n- {差別|さべつ}: discrimination (unfair treatment based on a characteristic)",
